INT. OFFICE PARK CONFERENCE ROOM "SERENITY" - MORNING

Glass walls. A whiteboard reading "Q3 SYNERGY LEVERAGE." A bowl of fruit nobody touches.

Six employees sit around a long table.

GARETH PLUMLEY-ADEBAYO (40s, regional vice president, loud socks) stands at the head, marker raised.

IFEOMA "IFE" KALUZA-BRENNER (30s, product lead) types without looking at the keyboard.

DESMOND "DEZ" MACALLISTER-TRAN (20s, intern, over-ironed shirt) holds a notebook like a hymnal.

PRUDENCE LOCKHART-OSEI (50s, compliance, red glasses) keeps her palms flat on the table.

WALTER "WALLY" ZIELINSKI-MAHMOUD (60s, facilities, tool belt) sits slightly apart, eating an apple.

HENRIETTA "HETTY" VASQUEZ-LINDGREN (30s, accountant) stares at the clock.

GARETH
Okay, team. Quick check-in. Ife, how are we feeling?

IFE
Aligned.

GARETH
Love that. Dez?

DEZ
Also aligned, sir.

GARETH
Call me Gareth.

DEZ
Yes, Mr. Plumley-Adebayo.

GARETH
Gareth.

DEZ
Gareth, sir.

PRUDENCE
Gareth, before we go further, I have to note that the budget memo is unsigned.

GARETH
Prudence, Prudence, Prudence.

PRUDENCE
That's my name.

GARETH
It will be signed.

HETTY
By whom?

GARETH
By... us.

WALLY
(chewing)
Nobody signs anything in this building. I've been here thirty years.

GARETH
Wally, great energy.

WALLY
It's an apple.

IFE
Gareth, the numbers--

GARETH
The numbers are flexible, Ife.

HETTY
Gareth, the numbers are literally negative three million.

GARETH
Hetty, what a strong, powerful negative.

A beat. The room hums. Dez writes "powerful negative" in his notebook and underlines it.

PRUDENCE
Gareth, this is a legal exposure.

GARETH
(brightly)
Team, let's pivot to appreciation.

He claps. Nobody joins. Walter finishes his apple. Places the core on the table, precisely in the center of the whiteboard's reflection.

WALLY
I'll tell you what I appreciate. The sprinklers work.

He takes a lighter from his tool belt and holds it under the smoke detector.

The sprinklers burst. Water pours over six faces. Gareth stands at the head, marker raised, dripping.

GARETH
(calmly)
Great. This is great.
